TUnit uses `[Before(…)]` / `[After(…)]` attributes with a `HookType` enum, plus class lifecycle interfaces. Here's a sketch for each scope:

---

### 1. Before / after every test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public void ResetDatabase()
    {
        InMemoryDb.Reset();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        InMemoryDb.Clear();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_IsCreated() { /* … */ }
}
```

---

### 2. Once before first / after last test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    private static HttpClient _client = null!;

    [Before(Class)]
    public static void StartFixture()
    {
        _client = new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri("http://localhost:5000") };
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static void DisposeFixture()
    {
        _client.Dispose();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task GetOrders_Returns200() { /* … */ }
}
```

> `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` methods **must be `static`**.

---

### 3. Once per assembly (before first / after last test in the assembly)

```csharp
public class WireMockSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static void StartWireMock()
    {
        WireMockServer.Start();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static void StopWireMock()
    {
        WireMockServer.Stop();
    }
}
```

The class can live anywhere in the assembly — TUnit discovers it by attribute.

---

### 4. Once for the entire test session (cross-assembly)

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static void ApplyMigrations()
    {
        DatabaseHelper.Migrate();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static void TearDown()
    {
        DatabaseHelper.Drop();
    }
}
```

---

### Quick reference

| Scope | Attribute | Method must be | Runs… |
|---|---|---|---|
| Per-test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | instance | around every `[Test]` |
| Per-class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | `static` | once per test class |
| Per-assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | `static` | once per assembly |
| Per-session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | `static` | once for entire run |

All hook methods can be `async Task` instead of `void`. The `HookType` values (`Test`, `Class`, `Assembly`, `TestSession`) come from `TUnit.Core`.
